{
  "name": "Cologne Cathedral",
  "_about": "COLOGNE CATHEDRAL from the same components as Notre-Dame (the `gothic` generator): the `basilica` nave, 43m to the vault, with wide double aisles, rib-vaulted; flying buttresses down both flanks and round the chevet; the west front under two 16m towers rising to a hundred metres, each crowned by an octagonal stage and an openwork spire to 157m (the `domed-tower`); a spiral stair in each tower up to the terrace the spire stands on.",
